      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why blindly modify OperStatus and ConnectStatus on reconcile? If an ONU was unreachable/unknown prior to reconcile, that state should be maintained after reconcile (unless the node has actually recovered). \nReconcile is called to do just that - reconcile the current state(s) with the existing state(s) in voltha core. In absence of any actual verification of operational and/or reachability state, the states should remain as they were prior to reconcile.\n\nIdeally we would verify operational and connect status via some form of OMCI messaging during reconcile but I realize that requires more investigation outside of this update.",
      "revId": "decdda8bf16476a41c28fe0bc44172a3f55d27f6",
